y shall equal the base facility rate.\nL13@P0: (3) The fee to be paid by a large storage facility shall equal twice the base facility rate.\nL14@P0: (4) The fee to be paid by a minitreatment facility shall equal 50 percent of the base\nL15@P0: facility rate.\nL16@P0: (5) The fee to be paid by a small treatment facility shall equal twice the base facility rate.\nL17@P0: (6) The fee to be paid by a large onsite treatment facility shall equal three times the base\nL18@P0: facility rate.\nL19@P0: (7) The fee to be paid by a large offsite treatment facility shall be three times the base\nL20@P0: facility rate.\nL21@P0: (8) The fee to be paid by a disposal facility shall equal 10 times the base facility rate.\nL22@P0: ( c) The fee to be paid by a facility with a postclosure permit during the first five years of the\nL23@P0: postclosure period shall be:\nL24@P0: (1) Four thousand five hundred seventy-eight dollars ($4,578)Twenty five thousand\nL25@P0: seven hundred fifty seven dollars ($25,757) annually for a small facility.\nL26@P0: (2) Nine thousand one hundred fifty-five dollars ($9.155) Fifty one thousand five hundred\nL27@P0: fifteen dollars ($51,515) annually for a medium facility.\nL28@P0: (3) Thirteen thousand seven hundred thirty-three dollars ($13,733) Seventy seven\nL29@P0: thousand two hundred seventy two dollars ($77,272) annually for a large facility.\nL30@P0: (d) The fee to be paid by a facility with a postclosure permit after the first five years of the\nL31@P0: postclosure care period shall be:\nL32@P0: (1) Two thousand four hundred thirty-nine dollars ($2,439) Thirteen thousand seven\nL33@P0: hundred twenty three dollars ($13,723) annually for a small facility.\nL34@P0: (2) Four thousand eight hundred seventy-eight dollars ($4,878)Twenty seven thousand\nL35@P0: four hundred forty seven dollars ($27,447) annually for a medium facility.\nL36@P0: (3) Eight thousand two hundred thirty-seven dollars ($8,237) Forty six: thousand three\nL37@P0: hundred fifty dollars ($46,350) annually for a large facility.\nL38@P0: (e) Notwithstanding subsection (b), the fee for a facility that has been issued a standardized\nL39@P0: permit shall be as follows:\nL40@P0-1: 1 Revised 9/24/26\nL41@P1: (1) The fee to be paid for a facility that has been issued a Series A standardized permit\nL42@P1: shall be nine thousand three hundred seventy-nine dollars ($9.379). fifty two\nL43@P1: thousand seven hundred seventy five dollars ($52,775).\nL44@P1: (2) The fee to be paid for a facility that has been issued a Series B standardized permit\nL45@P1: shall be four thousand three hundred ninety-six dollars ($4,396). twenty four\nL46@P1: thousand seven hundred thirty six dollars ($24,736).\nL47@P1: (3) Except as specified in paragraph (4), the fee to be paid for a facility that has been\nL48@P1: issued a Series C standardized permit shall be three thousand six hundred ninety\u0002two dollars ($3,692). twenty thousand seven hundred seventy four dollars ($20,774).\nL49@P1: (4) The fee for a facility that has been issued a Series C standardized permit is one\nL50@P1: thousand eight hundred forty-six dollars ($1,846) ten thousand three hundred eighty\nL51@P1: seven dollars ($10,387) if the facility meets all of the following conditions:\nL52@P1: A. The facility treats not more than 1,500 gallons of liquid hazardous waste and\nL53@P1: not more than 3,000 pounds of solid hazardous waste in any calendar month.\nL54@P1: B. The total facility storage capacity does not exceed 15,000 gallons of liquid\nL55@P1: hazardous waste and 30,000 pounds of solid hazardous waste.\nL56@P1: C. If the facility both treats and stores hazardous waste, the facility does not\nL57@P1: exceed the volume limitations specified in subparagraphs (A) and (B) for\nL58@P1: each individual activity.\nL59@P1: (f) (1) The fee for a facility or transportable treatment unit operating pursuant to a permit-by\u0002rule for the 2026-27 2025 26 fiscal year is seven hundred eighty dollars ($780). f